      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "CMBX10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 99,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p14_b7",
      "text": "Single dataset: Results are based on Alpaca instruction tuning; generalisation to other\nfine-tuning objectives (e.g., domain adaptation, RLHF) requires further study.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        328.63,
        523.53,
        353.18
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1314,
        2094,
        1412
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "CMBX10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 166,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p14_b8",
      "text": "Undertrained adapters: Despite loss reduction from \u223c2.0 to \u223c1.0, the adapters produce\noutputs identical to the base model on test prompts, suggesting the base model\u2019s strong priors\ndominate. This precludes causal validation via activation steering and is the primary limitation\nof the current work.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        361.13,
        523.34,
        412.83
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1444,
        2093,
        1651
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.02,
      "font_name": "CMBX10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 298,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p14_b9",
      "text": "SAE training scale: Delta SAEs are trained on \u223c1M token vectors. Larger-scale training may\nimprove reconstruction quality and alter the feature vocabulary.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        420.78,
        523.69,
        445.38
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1683,
        2094,
        1781
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 10.8,
      "font_name": "CMBX10",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 155,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.28896_p14_b10",
      "text": "No baseline comparison: We lack a base-base SAE similarity baseline (two independently\ntrained SAEs on base model activations), which would allow direct comparison to assess whether\n0.071 cosine similarity is genuinely low or attributable to SAE training variance. This is a\npriority for future work.\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        453.39,
        523.7,
        505.03
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
